  "scope": "The actual 1900-slot ordered demand scan traverses the stored original demand table, invokes the real original-row retained-matrix and zero-cost shortest-path machine for each visited demand, returns the first successful original occurrence pointer and its literal returned path, or allocates absence. All calls, saved contexts and recursive returns share one append-only heap. The exact raw demand/path fields equal original BinaryFractionalDispatch.findAvoiding applied to the original zeroMask. Its sum bound depends only on original graph, costs, labels and demands and includes physical terminal charge. Twelve actual physical interpreter cases independently check selection order, duplicate occurrence identity, absent paths, endpoint-specific masks, removed/retained interior vertices and padding. Zero masks are recomputed per visited demand in this implementation; equality is to the original result, not its logical operation counter. Original storage and width premises, initial preparation and outer dispatcher composition remain explicit.",
  "pending": [
    "independent semantic review",
    "combined production integration and exact CI"
  ]
